A | analysis-an-embed-resource-is-sized-by-the-librarys-reading-of-a-link | src/analysis/preprocess/preprocessor.cpp | tests/mutations/texts/analysis-an-embed-resource-is-sized-by-the-librarys-reading-of-a-link.before | tests/mutations/texts/analysis-an-embed-resource-is-sized-by-the-librarys-reading-of-a-link.after | TEST-RED | dsscp-lib | dss_analysis_preprocess_test_preprocessor | 532 | tests/mutations/texts/analysis-an-embed-resource-is-sized-by-the-librarys-reading-of-a-link.diag | CLAIM AT tests/analysis/preprocess/test_preprocessor.cpp, TEST FC179EmbedThroughALinkIsTheBytesTheLinkReaches. An #embed resource's byte count -- the width, if_empty and __has_embed all read it -- is the size of the file the path REACHES, asked of the substrate. Switched off (asked of the library: is_regular_file then file_size), the MinGW build sizes a file link by the link's own attributes, 0, so a resource reached through a link embeds NOTHING and __has_embed answers empty -- a silent miscompile; the MSVC and POSIX libraries follow the link and stay right.
